.SS "\fBsc_keyvalue_t\fP* sc_keyvalue_newf (int dummy,  \&.\&.\&.)"

.PP
Create a container and set one or more key-value pairs\&. Arguments come in pairs of 2: a static string 'type:key' and a value\&. The type is the letter i, g, s, p for int, double, const char *, and void *, respectively\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdummy\fP Not touched, just to use the varargs feature\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A key-value container initialized with the given entries\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBsc_keyvalue_t\fP* sc_keyvalue_newv (va_list ap)"

.PP
Create a container and set one or more key-value pairs\&. This function works analogously to \fBsc_keyvalue_newf\fP\&. Arguments come in pairs of 2: a static string 'type:key' and a value\&. The type is the letter i, g, s, p for int, double, const char *, and void *, respectively\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
